  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would result in the conversion of a single family residential dwelling where the site is located outside of an Area of Potential Intensification and the Gross Internal Area of the original dwelling is less than 125sqm. The proposal would therefore result in the loss of family housing without the provision of better-designed or higher-quality housing, contrary to the aims of Policy 10 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018. As such the proposed development is considered to be unacceptable in principle.",
    "The proposed development, by reason of the under provision of 3-bedroomed dwellings, would not provide a balanced mix of dwelling sizes and housing choice and would be contrary to Policy H10 of the London Plan 2021 and Policy 9 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The proposal fails to provide any private outdoor amenity space for the future occupants of the first floor flat, no double or twin rooms are provided in the ground floor flat, one of the bedrooms within the ground floor unit falls below the minimum floor area required for a single bedroom and another bedroom does not have any outlook. This is contrary to the aims of Policy D6 of the London Plan and Policy 9 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.\r\r\r",
    "The applicant has failed to provide a Parking Stress Survey (Lambeth Methodology) to demonstrate that the proposed development, which provides no off-street parking, would not result in an unacceptable increase in on-street parking demand. Given the site's PTAL rating of 2 (Poor), there is a requirement for on-site parking provision or robust evidence to justify a car-free approach. In the absence of such evidence, the proposal is considered to hinder the free flow of traffic and compromise highway safety, contrary to Sutton Local Plan Policies 36 and 37."
  ],
